Independent verifier: proven. opendeck/ implements every sub-claim. (1) Stream Deck connection: plugin.js connects via loopback WebSocket and registers with the host's register event. (2) Per-agent buttons: render.js puts one key per project (6 on Mini main page, menu page for >6), each rendered by keyart.projectKey. (3) RAG colors: STATE_COLOR maps running=green/working, idle=amber/idle, waiting=red/asking a question, off=gray/no connected env; stateFor derives state from /session/status (explicit status wins) or update recency; test/sessions.test.js pins these. (4) Gray when no env: fetchSessions returns ok:false when the opencode server is unreachable and projects with no live session render OFF/gray. (5) Auto-update on launch: 5s poller (POLL_MS) re-fetches /session; poll() mints an auto-project for sessions in unconfigured directories (persisted via writeAutoProjects) and calls renderAll(), so launching opencode auto-shows its button. (6) Press-to-focus: handleProjectPress single-tap calls focusSession({marker:`opencode:<alias>`}; focus.js raises the terminal window whose title contains the marker via EnumWindows/SetForegroundWindow (Windows), with fallback to activating the terminal; launchProject spawns opencode-3090-serve.bat in a new Windows Terminal tab titled [opencode:<alias>] opencode; double-tap launches a parallel session. (7) OpenCode not Claude: deck polls the `opencode serve` HTTP server (127.0.0.1:4096 per projects.json); grep finds zero 'claude' in opendeck/. (8) No model/backend touching: deck is read-only (GET /session, GET /session/status) and only manipulates terminal windows; no vLLM/llama.cpp/SGLang/vision or model code in the deck. Shipped bundle dev.ryans.opendeck.streamDeckPlugin (manifest + bin/plugin.mjs + imgs) exists and mirrors source. Host evidence (3 turns, 50 mutations) corroborates execution this revision. Evidence: opendeck/src/sessions.js: // RAG state (the user's requirement):
//   green  = working   (opencode is actively generating / running a tool)
